- <span id="page-48-8"></span>[F332] References in this Regulation to the processing of personal data for the purposes of scientific research (including references to processing for "scientific research purposes") are references to processing for the purposes of any research that can reasonably be described as scientific, whether publicly or privately funded and whether carried out as a commercial or non-commercial activity.
- 3 Such references
  - a include processing for the purposes of technological development or demonstration, fundamental research or applied research, so far as those activities can reasonably be described as scientific, but
  - b only include processing for the purposes of a study in the area of public health that can reasonably be described as scientific where the study is conducted in the public interest.
