- (4) to impose fees, maintenance fees, compensation, or service fees for the Office's operations according to the Office's objectives, in accordance with the criteria and at the rate specified by the Office, with the approval of the commission supervising the Office of Personal Data ProtectionCommittee;

(5) to carry out any other acts that the law specifies to be the duties and powers of the Office, or as assigned by the Committee, the commission supervising the Office of Personal Data Protection Committee, the expert committee, orthe sub-committee.

